%   primary source for what the functions do.
% QUOTE (sec. 7.2): "It is good practice to use the with keyword when
%   dealing with file objects. The advantage is that the file is
%   properly closed after its suite finishes, even if an exception is
%   raised at some point."  "If you're not using the with keyword, then
%   you should call f.close() to close the file and immediately free up
%   any system resources used by it."  "Warning Calling f.write()
